 *   **Boundaries:** Ensure loops respect the chunk boundaries ($0$ to $CHUNK\_SIZE-1$) to avoid out-of-bounds memory access [S3, unofficial].
 *   **Degenerate Input:** Empty chunks should be skipped entirely to avoid unnecessary draw calls [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Performance:** Using very small voxels results in very small triangles, which consume significant GPU resources [S2, unofficial]. Performance suffers greatly when increasing platform size because it uploads and draws $36 \times \text{voxel\_count}$ vertices every frame [S5, unofficial]. Extremely slow and memory intensive; can crash the kernel or cause swapping issues with large datasets [S8, unofficial].
 
